# The manager build context is the repository root, and the Dockerfile copies
# exactly five things: go.mod, go.sum, api/, cmd/, internal/. Everything else —
# the chart, the docs, openspec, every sibling module, .git — was being uploaded
# to the daemon on every build for nothing.
#
# EXCLUDE-THEN-REINCLUDE, deliberately. A denylist has to name every module
# directory, so module number fourteen silently rejoins the context on the day
# it is added. This form is what the release matrices are: derived from what the
# build actually needs, not from a list somebody has to remember to edit.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!api/
!cmd/
!internal/

# ...and nothing under those that the build has no use for.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
